																		Rewrite Attribution and Other Matters
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2039383&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606207819" alt="MrWrong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2039383)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;" >MrWrong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1433816452 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Jun 2015 02:20</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2313553">
									

<p>This article is a rewrite of a previous iteration of SCP-2144 by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/schrodingers-kitty" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2137696); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2137696&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1434419433" alt="Schrodingers_Kitty" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2137696)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/schrodingers-kitty" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2137696); return false;">Schrodingers_Kitty</a></span> (original Author of the work). I would also like to thank the Rewrite Team (chiefly Decibelles, who was my main contact) for the opportunity to rewrite this article.</p>
<p>This is inspired by my experiences in Junior College, where I initially thought Schrodinger's Cat as a literal concept.</p>
<p>So what's going on?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCP-2144 is a literal Schrodinger's Cat.</p>
<p>Whatever Mel is, she's the same class of beings as SCP-990. Sentient dream-beings.</p>
<p>SCP-2144 is effectively a thought-form, a &quot;brainchild&quot; of Mel and Jason that is half memetic and half &quot;realised&quot;. That was partially inspired by the Percy Jackson series' concept of a &quot;child of Athena&quot; who are effectively &quot;brainchildren&quot;.</p>
<p>As to its odd features of its heart rate slowing to potentially death, I would say that it is the fact that it is a flawed idea – it's no meant to be a thing. It's sort of a corrective impulse (or &quot;instinct&quot;) to set things right by sending itself towards death.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

