			<div class="content" id="post-content-2313717">
									

<p>A few small comments:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Seek</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;And&nbsp;you&nbsp;shall&nbsp;find</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Once per month, the enclosure's structural integrity is to be inspected by a containment engineer. If any damage to the enclosure is identified, a containment engineer is to repair said damage.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This didn't seem to relate to the cat's anomalous properties - it's not causing particular damage to the enclosure, and any damage won't cause it to release the gas. Wouldn't general structural inspections be part of standard (rather than special) containment procedures?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An observation post is to be established along the perimeter of the enclosure, with transceivers placed in each post. At all times, a guard is to be stationed in the observation post to watch over SCP-2144. An auxiliary group of up to 3 guards are to be put on standby, in case the assigned guard is unavailable for observation duty. Guards on duty are to rotate in shifts of 2 hours apiece; see Document 2144-Ø for observation duty schedule. At the beginning of each shift, the guard on duty is to acknowledge SCP-2144's presence via transceiver.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>While observation of the cat is presumably part of the reference, I felt that this was a little longer than it needed to be. Are the transceivers, standby guards and duty schedules necessary?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An observation post &#8230; in each post.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is there one post, or more than one?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>weighing scales</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd suggest just &quot;scales&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>personnel who had held SCP-2144 estimates it to weigh</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;personnel who have held SCP-2144 estimate that it weighs&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Its heartbeat can only be detected under such a state, along with signs of respiration.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Its heartbeat and respiration can be detected only while in this state.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Furthermore, SCP-2144's image and sounds can only be photographed and recorded in this state.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Furthermore, it is only in this state that SCP-2144's image can be photographed.&quot; If the cat ceases all movement in &quot;dead&quot; phase, presumably it isn't making sounds?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Its anomalous properties were revealed when it resumes motion when taken out of the residence.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;when it resumed motion after removal from the residence&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Jason Schmidt is capable of lucid dreaming and has a habit to record details of his dreams</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Jason is dead, so I suggest &quot;Jason Schmidt was capable of lucid dreaming and habitually recorded details of his dreams&quot;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Summary: this is a nice iterative improvement, keeping the bones of the original idea. A little too much of what feels like filler in the procedures is keeping it from an upvote from my perspective.</p>

							</div>

								
					
